# ── Worksheet DETAIL page trailing-slash handling ──
# NOTE (2026-07-22): Removed the forced "301!" trailing-slash → no-slash rules
# that previously lived here. Because index.html exists at the slash path AND
# Netlify's default pretty-URL handling canonicalizes trailing slashes on its
# own, forcing the opposite redirect created a redirect cycle
# (slash → no-slash → slash …), which surfaced to visitors as
# "numberbender.com redirected you too many times" (ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS),
# especially for returning visitors whose browsers had cached the redirects.
#
# Canonicalization is now handled without a forced redirect: every worksheet
# page carries <link rel="canonical"> to its no-slash URL, the sitemap lists
# only the no-slash form, and all internal links point to the no-slash form.
#
# UPDATE (2026-10): the slash form now 301s to the no-slash form site-wide via
# netlify/edge-functions/trailing-slash.js, which sees the raw path and so
# can't loop the way a rule here did. Don't add slash rules back to this file.

